------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <RangeSlider> is a PURE presentational PRIMITIVE — a CONTROLLED dual-thumb input whose `value` +
`onChange` are plain props. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading /
error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from; a host owns the
value). Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface
reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the sibling presentational primitives
Accordion (0203), Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095), InlineCallout (0124), ActiveFilterChips (0147), and
StaggerItem (0194) used. The REAL branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • enabled              : track ground + selected-range fill + two draggable, VoiceOver-adjustable thumbs.
  • disabled             : both thumbs non-interactive + dimmed; setLow/setHigh/step are no-ops, no emit.
  • label shown / hidden : web showLabel — the label + tabular-nums "low – high" caption row, or track only.
  • thumb-swap (both)    : low past high -> [high,next]; high below low -> [next,low] (web handleLow/High).
  • fill span            : left=min(lowPct,highPct), right=max(...); accent@0.6 (web cyan-500/60).
  • colliding z-order    : web lowPct>50 -> low thumb raised, else high raised (grabbable near an edge).
  • value format         : web formatValue ?? String(n) (integral drops decimals); custom formatter honored.
  • thumb a11y names     : web minThumbLabel/maxThumbLabel ?? t('slider.thumbMin/Max','{{label}} …').
  • degenerate range     : native never-a-blank-box affordance when max<=min (web renders a full immovable
                           track; native states the condition). Percents still use the web 0/100 fallback.
  • reduced motion       : fill / thumb travel animate via easeOut(fast); nil (instant) under reduce.
Data source  : none (pure presentational; value is controlled interaction state, not fetched) — web hooks
               were `useTranslation` (P1/S10 facade) + `useId` (native a11y elements replace the DOM ids).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none; it composes two raw <input type=range> + a Caption span).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : slider.thumbMin + slider.thumbMax mirrored verbatim from source; rangeConnector/empty/
               emptyMessage are native a11y/HIG additions; ALL resolved through the P1/S10 facade.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "RangeSlider" (P1/S11).
a11y         : each thumb is its own adjustable element with an explicit label (web ariaLow/ariaHigh) +
               value (displayLow/displayHigh) + AccessibilityAdjustableAction (Arrow/swipe steps by `step`,
               the WAI-ARIA APG slider pattern); track ground/fill hidden; 44pt hit targets; reduce-motion
               honored; Dynamic Type via tokens; label row + empty leaf are single combined elements.

